                "text": "As of early February, San Francisco's Department of Homelessness and Supportive Housing reported 1,633 unhoused people approved for supportive housing and awaiting their turn to move in — despite 888 vacancies in its permanent supportive housing stock as of Feb. 22. Filling those empty rooms would cut the waiting list by more than half, and house roughly 1 in every 8 homeless people in the city.",
